%I A399678 #24 Sep 29 2026 23:37:06
%S A399678 1,1,6,41,345,3892,134462
%N A399678 Number of nonisomorphic commutative doppelsemigroups of order n.
%C A399678 A doppelsemigroup is an algebraic structure (D,-|,|-) consisting of a set D equipped with two associative binary operations -| and |- satisfying the following axioms: (x-|y)|-z=x-|(y|-z) and (x|-y)-|z=x|-(y-|z).
%C A399678 A doppelsemigroup (D,-|,|-) is called commutative if both component semigroups (D,-|) and (D,|-) are commutative.
%H A399678 V.M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.15421/242602">Note on the number of doppelsemigroups of small order</a>, Res. Math. 34(1) (2026), 16-33.
%H A399678 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22639886">Lists of All Pairwise Nonisomorphic Commutative Doppelsemigroups of Orders up to 6</a>.
%H A399678 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://gist.github.com/vgavrylkiv/bdf06def09430abfb06a4c16ee0baa95">Python code for computing nonisomorphic doppelsemigroups</a>.
%e A399678 For n = 2, there are exactly 6 nonisomorphic commutative doppelsemigroups (D,-|,|-) on the set D={0,1}. Rows and columns are ordered as 0,1. The Cayley tables of all six doppelsemigroups are listed below.
%e A399678 Doppelsemigroup #1:
%e A399678   -|:   |-:
%e A399678   0 0   0 0
%e A399678   0 0   0 0
%e A399678 Doppelsemigroup #2:
%e A399678   -|:   |-:
%e A399678   0 0   0 0
%e A399678   0 0   0 1
%e A399678 Doppelsemigroup #3:
%e A399678   -|:   |-:
%e A399678   0 1   0 1
%e A399678   1 0   1 0
%e A399678 Doppelsemigroup #4:
%e A399678   -|:   |-:
%e A399678   0 1   1 0
%e A399678   1 0   0 1
%e A399678 Doppelsemigroup #5:
%e A399678   -|:   |-:
%e A399678   0 0   0 0
%e A399678   0 1   0 0
%e A399678 Doppelsemigroup #6:
%e A399678   -|:   |-:
%e A399678   0 0   0 0
%e A399678   0 1   0 1
%Y A399678 Cf. A399676, A399679, A027851, A001426.
